  "facts": [
    "The Willis Avenue Bridge, a 1901 swing bridge, once carried trolley tracks, which were installed in 1916 after a retrofit to support heavy Union Railway Company cars.",
    "During the 2010 NYC Marathon, runners cross the Willis Avenue Bridge at the 20‑mile mark, earning the nickname “the wall” before heading into the Bronx.",
    "In 2007, the city replaced the aging bridge with a new 350‑foot structure shipped from Albany, a $417‑million project that became the most expensive DOT construction effort in New York City history."
